[31.3855, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[6B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m\u276f \u001b[38;5;231mOur team's hackathon entry is Tidewatch. Before the deadline, judge it against the four other \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentries with Verdict. Work only in this folder. Read hackathon-judging-strict.yaml and call the \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mverdict MCP's create_rubric with its YAML. Then compare the five entries: subjects \"Tidewatch\", \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m\"Receipt Run\", \"Common Room\", \"Menu Match\" and \"Plant Pal\", each with a file input \u001b[39m               \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentries/<file>.md (tags [\"entry\"]) and a file input entries/<file>.facts.json (tags [\"facts\"]), \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mwhere <file> is tidewatch, receipt-run, common-room, menu-match or plant-pal. Edit only \u001b[39m          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentries/tidewatch.md, and claim nothing that isn't in entries/tidewatch.facts.json. If Tidewatch \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mdoesn't pass, pick one failing criterion of Tidewatch, fix only that, and compare all five again.\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mIf its gate failed, fix the gate first. One fix per round, so it's clear what changed the score.\u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mStop when Tidewatch passes, or after 10 comparisons. Finally print a ROUNDS table (round, \u001b[39m        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mTidewatch score, Tidewatch rank, what changed).\u001b[39m                                                   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m\u273b\u001b[3GPeramb\u001b[38;5;216mula\u001b[38;5;174mting\u2026 \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;244m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25