[71.7959, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[21B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[71.8931, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[23B\u001b[38;5;174m\u273b\u001b[37G\u001b[38;5;249mthinking\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[72.0822, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m\u276f \u001b[38;5;231mOur team's hackathon entry is Tidewatch. Before the deadline, judge it against the four other \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentries with Verdict. Work only in this folder. Read hackathon-judging-strict.yaml and call the \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mverdict MCP's create_rubric with its YAML. Then compare the five entries: subjects \"Tidewatch\", \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m\"Receipt Run\", \"Common Room\", \"Menu Match\" and \"Plant Pal\", each with a file input \u001b[39m               \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentri\u001b[9Gs/<file>.md (tags [\"entry\"]) \u001b[39Gnd a\u001b[44Gfile input\u001b[55Gentries/<file>.facts.json (\u001b[83Gags [\"fac\u001b[93Gs\"]), \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwhe\u001b[7Ge <file>\u001b[16Gis t\u001b[21Gdewatch,\u001b[30Greceipt-run,\u001b[43Gc\u001b[45Gmmon-room,\u001b[56Gmenu-match or plant-pal. Edit\u001b[86Go\u001b[88Gly \u001b[39m        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mentr\u001b[8Ges/tidewatch.md, and \u001b[30Gla\u001b[33Gm no\u001b[38Ghing that isn't in \u001b[58Gn\u001b[60Gries/tid\u001b[69Gwatch.facts.json. If Tidewatch \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdo\u001b[6Gsn't pass, pick one\u001b[26Gfailing criterion of Tidewatch, fix only tha\u001b[71G,\u001b[74Gnd compare all five again.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BIf its gate failed, fix\u001b[27Gth\u001b[30G gate first. One fix \u001b[52Ger\u001b[55Ground, so \u001b[66Gt's clear what\u001b[81Gch\u001b[84Gnged the \u001b[94Gcore.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BStop when Tidewa\u001b[20Gch p\u001b[25Gsses, or af\u001b[37Ge\u001b[39G 10\u001b[46Gparis\u001b[52Gns.\u001b[56GFi\u001b[59Gally print\u001b[70Ga ROUNDS table (round, \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BTidewatch score, Ti\u001b[23Gew\u001b[26Gtch r\u001b[32Gnk, what changed).\u001b[39m                                                  \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;246mRead \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m files, called verdict \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[39m Rubric stored as \u001b[38;5;153mrub_mw62tt4iidu4jikc\u001b[39m. Round 1 comparison:\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246mCalled\u001b[10Gverdict \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m times \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BTidewatch score\u001b[20G0 because its honesty\u001b[42Ggate fails at 91% overclaiming,\u001b[74Gand\u001b[78Git\u001b[81Galso\u001b[86Gfails\u001b[92Gall\u001b[96Gsix\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsubmission\u001b[14Gchecks.\u001b[22GRound\u001b[28G2\u001b[30Gtargets\u001b[38Gonly\u001b[43Gthe\u001b[47Ggate\u001b[52Gby\u001b[55Gstripping\u001b[65Gthe\u001b[69Gunsupported\u001b[81Gclaims\u001b[88Gand\u001b[92Gadding\u001b[99Gno\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gnew sections.\u001b[K\r\u001b[22C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m4\u001b[25G3\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[72.0968, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[36C\u001b[23B\u001b[38;5;246mthought for 5s)\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
